Discussion

The team reviewed the Week 3 requirement to enhance the existing Week 2 simulator with Memory, Stack and FIFO Queue functionality.
The team agreed that completed Week 2 functionality should not be rewritten unnecessarily.
Memory will be extended with Read/Write operations and integrated with the simulator.
Stack work will focus on Stack Pointer (SP), PUSH and POP operations.
A FIFO Queue will be added with ENQUEUE and DEQUEUE operations, including empty/full handling.
A Queue flowchart, processor-specific Assembly validation program, expected/actual results and test documentation will also be prepared.

Decisions

1. Keep the existing Week 2 implementation and add only the required Week 3 functionality.
2. Use `Queue.java` as the new FIFO Queue module.
3. Integrate the new modules with the existing CPU and UI instead of creating a separate simulator.
4. Document the four new Week 3 instructions: PUSH, POP, ENQUEUE and DEQUEUE with examples and outputs.
5. Maintain Week 3 test cases and validation results in the Docs folder.

